Her academic research specializes in behavioral science and decision-making.</description></item><item><title>Ricardo Guzmán</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/ricardo-guzman/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/ricardo-guzman/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Juan Pablo Couyoumdjian</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/juan-pablo-couyoumdjian/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/juan-pablo-couyoumdjian/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Carlos Rodríguez</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/carlos-rodriguez/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/carlos-rodriguez/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Mauricio Apablaza</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/mauricio-apablaza/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/mauricio-apablaza/</guid><description/></item><item><title>María Paz Raveau</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/maria-paz-raveau/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/maria-paz-raveau/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Aníbal Olivera</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/anibal-olivera/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/anibal-olivera/</guid><description>Aníbal Olivera is a Ph.D. student in Social Complexity Sciences, funded by an ANID National Doctoral Scholarship. He previously trained in Physics at the Universidad de Concepción, where he earned a B.Sc. in Physics and an M.Sc. in Physics.
His research studies how the structure of social networks shapes the diffusion and abandonment of behaviors. In Networks Decide for Us he imputes homophilous networks onto representative surveys to measure how much of diffusion is due to topology; in Network Disadoption he proposes a measure of exposure to neighbors who abandon a behavior; and in Political Networks he analyzes collaboration among members of Chile&amp;rsquo;s 2021-2022 Constitutional Convention.</description></item><item><title>Constanza Pino</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/constanza-pino/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/constanza-pino/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Francisco Villarroel</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/francisco-villarroel/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/francisco-villarroel/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Alejandra Molina</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/alejandra-molina/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/alejandra-molina/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Camila Utreras</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/camila-utreras/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/camila-utreras/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Pedro Ávila</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/pedro-avila/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/pedro-avila/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Carlos Hidalgo</title><link>https://policics.github.io/en/team/carlos-hidalgo/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Jan 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://policics.github.io/en/team/carlos-hidalgo/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>